        answer: "Depreciation recapture is the portion of gain taxed at ordinary federal income rates, up to the amount of depreciation deductions claimed, rather than at long term capital gains rates. In a completed 1031 exchange, recapture is deferred along with the capital gain, carried forward in the replacement property's lower carryover basis rather than taxed immediately.",
